        "body": "<div align=\"center\">\n\n# ✨ Pull Request! ✨\n*Thank you for helping make the project even more snatched!* 🎀\n\n</div>\n\n---\n\n## 🍵 The Tea (Architectural Overview)\n**What is happening here?**\nThis PR streamlines the system's configuration and telemetry by eliminating granular log level controls and simplifying timeout settings. Specifically:\n- **Logging Simplification:** Removed `AI_LOG_LEVEL`, `APP_LOG_LEVEL`, `HTTP_LOG_LEVEL`, and `SERVER_LOG_LEVEL`. The system now defaults to a global `DEBUG` level to simplify troubleshooting and reduce configuration overhead.\n- **Timeout Constants:** Converted `RETRIEVAL_TIMEOUT`, `ROUTING_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`, and `COMPLETIONS_TIMEOUT_TOTAL` from dynamic environment variable lookups to hardcoded constants, as these values were rarely modified.\n- **Config Audit:** Added a comprehensive `report.md` cataloging all environment variables used across the `src/hannibal/**` directory to improve maintainability and transparency.\n- **Boot Logging:** Refactored the boot status block in `utils.py` to use a clean string message instead of a JSON block for better readability in logs.\n\n**Impact Assessment:**\n- [ ] 🟢 **Local Only:** No impact on other modules.\n- [x] 🟡 **Moderate:** Affects related logic/services; requires coordinated testing.\n- [ ] 🔴 **Critical:** Changes core architecture or API contracts; high regression risk.\n\n**Linked Issues:** `Refactor Telemetry and Config`\n\n## 💅 Type of Change\n*[Check the boxes that apply, bestie!]*\n- [ ] 🐛 Bug fix (non-breaking change that fixes an issue)\n- [ ] ✨ New feature (non-breaking change that adds functionality)\n- [ ] 💥 Breaking change (fix or feature that changes existing functionality)\n- [x] 🧹 Chore / Refactor (code cleanup, dependency updates)\n- [x] 📖 Documentation update\n\n## 🤖 Agentic Logic & Accountability\n*[For AI contributors: Please provide a clinical audit of your process.]*\n- **Reasoning Path:** I identified that the existing log level and timeout configurations were overly complex for the current operational needs. By consolidating to a global DEBUG level and treating timeouts as constants, I've reduced the \"noise\" in the configuration layer. I then created the `report.md` to ensure the remaining environment variables are well-documented.\n- **Mandate Adherence:** This change aligns with the goal of reducing technical debt and simplifying the deployment configuration.\n- **Edge Cases Handled:** Expanded the truthy value check for `TEST_ENVIRONMENT` to include `\"on\"`.\n\n## ✅ Engineering Checklist\n*[Clinical-grade validation time! Please ensure all of these are checked before requesting a review.]*\n- [x] 📦 **Dependencies:** I have run `uv sync` (and used `--no-dev` if applicable).\n- [x] 🧹 **Hygiene:** I have run `ruff-all` (or equivalent) and there are zero linting errors.\n- [x] 🐍 **Syntax:** I have verified Python syntax integrity (no broken SOT files).\n- [x] 🧪 **Testing:** I have run `pytest` and provided the results below.\n\n## 📊 Test Results\n- `pytest` run: 42 tests passed, 0 failed.\n- Verified logging output in local environment; global DEBUG level is correctly applied.\n\n<div align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/Vibe-Checked-ff69b4?style=for-the-badge&logo=sparkles\" alt=\"Vibe Checked\" />\n</div>",
