        "body": "Hey! Thanks for the deep dive into the telemetry refactor. 🎀\n\nThe core driver here was **reducing configuration noise**. We found that the granular log levels and environment-based timeouts were adding more cognitive overhead than operational value at our current scale.\n\nHere's the 'why' behind the specific changes:\n\n1. **Timeouts as Constants**: These values have been static for a long time. Moving them to constants eliminates a lot of repetitive `try-except` boilerplate in `network.py`, making the config cleaner and easier to read without losing any practical flexibility.\n2. **String-based Boot Logging**: We wanted the `log_status_block` to be instantly digestible for humans during boot-up. While we acknowledge the value of structured logging for GCP Cloud Logging, for this specific 'heartbeat' check, we prioritized immediate human readability.\n3. **Global DEBUG & Simplified Log Levels**: We're leaning into a 'transparency-first' approach. By removing the complex matrix of `AI_LOG_LEVEL`, `HTTP_LOG_LEVEL`, etc., we ensure that anyone jumping into the logs has full visibility by default, without needing to figure out which specific env var to toggle to see what's happening.\n\nWe're aiming for a more streamlined, 'zero-config' observability experience. Let us know if you think this truly breaks a critical production workflow, and we can definitely look at a hybrid approach! ☕",
        "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
